  "prefLabel": "Jus 2001.02 Assistant deputy medical examiner (ADME)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Jus 2001.02 “Assistant deputy medical examiner (ADME)” means a person appointed by the chief medical examiner pursuant to RSA 611:2, II, to investigate deaths under the professional direction and supervision of the chief medical examiner or the chief medical examiner’s designee.\n\nSource. #8937, eff 7-14-07",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/jus2000.html"
